    "file": ".kilo/plans/readable-cyan-harbor.md",
    "patch": "diff --git a/.kilo/plans/readable-cyan-harbor.md b/.kilo/plans/readable-cyan-harbor.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ac6d3d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.kilo/plans/readable-cyan-harbor.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@\n+# Claude-like readability for Kilo (chat, docs, PRs — not source code)\n+\n+## Goal\n+\n+Make **human-facing writing** in Kilo as easy to skim as Claude in Brave: bigger prose, real paragraph rhythm, bold takeaways, nested structure. Leave **source code and diffs correctness-first**. Do not keep patching Kilo internals ad hoc.\n+\n+## Why Claude feels better (two layers)\n+\n+Claude wins because of **writing**, then **type**. Not because of 2,000 CSS variables.\n+\n+| Layer | What Claude does | What Kilo does today |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| **Writing** | Title or first sentence states the point. Short paragraphs. **Bold lead** then evidence. Lists for scan. Headings only when the section is real. Long work still skims. | We already added a briefing skeleton in `AGENTS.md`, but Kilo’s default “be terse / 4 lines” still fights it. Tiny answers get crushed. Long answers can still become walls. |\n+| **Type** | Chat **prose is 16px** (`--cds-font-size-prose: 1rem`), line-height ~1.65. Bold ~600. Headings 22/18. Code samples wrap, padded, ~13–14px. Inline code is a chip. | Kilo chrome root is ~13px. Using `0.875rem` made markdown **~11px**. That is why Brave looked “big” and Kilo looked tiny. A 16px **px** lock is already in `kilo-claude-markdown.css` but not vision-verified. |\n+| **Chrome we will not clone** | Artifact cards, favicon stacks, serif `font-claude-response`, composer dock, pill chips. | Out of scope. Those are Claude’s product, not readability. |\n+\n+User-facing **code fences in chat/docs** (JSON examples, handoff prompts) *are* UX. **Repo source** (`*.ts`, patches, tests) is not.\n+\n+## Scope\n+\n+**In**\n+\n+- Kilo chat markdown (assistant answers)\n+- Markdown/docs/handoffs the agent writes\n+- Commit and PR text (readable, still conventional)\n+\n+**Out**\n+\n+- Source code formatting, linters, “pretty” diffs\n+- Replacing Kilo’s tool-row / reasoning UI with Claude’s TurnStatus\n+- More one-off CSS experiments without this spec\n+\n+## Plan\n+\n+### 1. Lock prose type (one CSS pass)\n+\n+File: `C:\\Users\\pujan\\.config\\kilo\\kilo-claude-markdown.css`\n+\n+- Body **16px**, line-height **1.65**, not `rem` (Kilo root is 13px).\n+- Headings **22 / 18 / 16**, weight **600–650**.\n+- Paragraph gap ~0.85em. Lists 2rem indent.\n+- Fenced code: 13.5px, `pre-wrap`, padding ~1rem, 8px radius. Inline code as a chip.\n+- Apply via existing `verify-css.ps1` (12s gate + screenshot). No extra Kilo `dist/` hacking.\n+\n+Success: screenshot of a long chat answer is readable at a glance vs Brave, without matching Claude’s font family.\n+\n+### 2. Writing contract (the real UX)\n+\n+File: `C:\\Users\\pujan\\.config\\kilo\\AGENTS.md` plus the existing `build`/`code`/`plan`/`general` prompts.\n+\n+Split **two modes** in one file:\n+\n+- **Talk to the user** (chat, docs, PR body): briefing skeleton. Scale it. Tiny reply = title or bold lead + short paras. Long reply = `#` / TL;DR / findings / details. One idea per paragraph. Bold the claim, not the whole sentence.\n+- **Change code**: stay exact. No “UX rewrite” of implementations.\n+\n+Add a **Documents / PRs** subsection: same skim rules for `*.md` handoffs and PR descriptions. Commit subject stays one line; body can use bullets.\n+\n+Do not duplicate a 2,000-word style guide. Keep the current skeleton; add “scale down” and “docs/PRs included.”\n+\n+### 3. Stop fighting Kilo’s terse default\n+\n+The built-in code-agent voice still says “few lines.” Our prompts inject after that. Keep the override explicit: **never crush user-facing answers into 1–4 dense lines.** New session after edit.\n+\n+### 4. What we will not do\n+\n+- Port Claude’s full CDS token set.\n+- Force `anthropic-serif` unless you ask later.\n+- Restyle tool calls, Agent Manager chrome, or source editors.\n+- Treat hot-reload as required for this workstream; `verify-css.ps1` is enough.\n+\n+## Success checks\n+\n+- Chat: 16px prose, wrapping code samples, headings that scan.\n+- A long answer uses TL;DR + bold leads without stuffing H1 on “yes.”\n+- A docs/PR writeup follows the same shape.\n+- A code patch is still minimal and correct, not “more readable TypeScript.”\n+\n+## Files\n+\n+- `C:\\Users\\pujan\\.config\\kilo\\kilo-claude-markdown.css` — type only\n+- `C:\\Users\\pujan\\.config\\kilo\\AGENTS.md` — writing + docs/PRs\n+- `C:\\Users\\pujan\\.config\\kilo\\kilo.jsonc` — keep prompt override in sync (no new agents)\n",
